SDL2_68k fixes for AmigaOS 3 on the PiStorm, from arczi84's patch (GitHub
issue 5 of ladislawv/ogles2, gist 18ddb47cc9059dd7cf6c6842e58bf6d5), on top
of 0001 and src/:
- Makefile: no -DSDL_OS3_DEBUG (SDL wrote WORK:sdl_log.txt and
  WORK:sdl_debug.log, from subtasks and under Forbid: a requester on systems
  without a WORK: volume);
- AHI audio: SDL's audio thread holds the message port while it runs, so
  WaitIO there gets the replies (silence, then noise, before); ogles2
  changed arczi84's version from taking the port at the first I/O to
  ThreadInit/ThreadDeinit, so a reply after the thread ends signals the
  opening task, not a task that is gone;
- AHI audio (ogles2's, found testing the above on the A1200): the
  availability check opens AHI_NO_UNIT, not unit 0 (unit 0 opened, closed
  and opened again at once left AHI 6.7 there never completing the first
  write: the thread hung);
- fullscreen on PiStorm RTG: a 32-bit mode of the size asked for, from the
  display database (BestCModeIDTags with depth 32 finds none there);
- the display's driverdata, so the screen SetDisplayMode opens is recorded
  and closed (each fullscreen run left a blank "SDL" screen), and the
  desktop mode is the Workbench (no new screen);
- rawkeys 0x64/0x65 are Alt and 0x66/0x67 Amiga (they were swapped).

